---
import LocalNav from '../../components/LocalNav.astro';
import EventFooter from '../../components/EventFooter.astro';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-IN" dir="ltr">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
        <title>Terms of Use - AAAI Event Hub</title>
        <meta name="Description" content="The terms of use for the AAAI Event Hub website and event — acceptance, acceptable use, intellectual property, liability and more." />
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/fonts.css" />
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/ac-localnav.built.css" />
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/event-pages.css" />
    </head>
    <body>
        <LocalNav current="legal" />
        <main class="event-main">
            <header class="event-hero">
                <p class="eyebrow">AAAI Event Hub</p>
                <h1>Terms of Use.</h1>
                <p class="subhead">The ground rules for using this website and joining the event — short, plain and fair.</p>
            </header>

            <section class="event-section on-white" aria-label="Terms of use">
                <div class="event-container prose">
                    <p class="prose-meta">Last updated: 1 August 2026</p>

                    <h2>1. Acceptance of these terms</h2>
                    <p>By accessing this website or attending the AAAI Event Hub, you agree to these Terms of Use, our <a href="/legal/sales-policy/">Sales Policy</a>, our <a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and our house guidelines. If you don't agree, please don't use the site or attend the event.</p>

                    <h2>2. Changes to these terms</h2>
                    <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The current version is always published on this page with its last-updated date, and material changes are announced on the website ahead of the event.</p>

                    <h2>3. Using our website</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Use the site lawfully and respectfully. Don't attempt to breach, probe or disrupt its security or availability.</li>
                        <li>Don't scrape, republish or resell content from the site without written permission.</li>
                        <li>Don't misrepresent your identity or affiliation when registering or contacting us.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
                    <p>All content on this website — text, design, graphics, logos, audio and video — is owned by AAAI Inc. or licensed to us, and protected by applicable laws. You may view and share links freely; everything else requires permission.</p>

                    <h2>5. Passes &amp; attendance</h2>
                    <p>Purchasing a pass is subject to our Sales Policy. Attending the event means following our code of conduct and house guidelines at all times. We may refuse entry or revoke a pass, without refund, for serious or repeated breaches.</p>

                    <h2>6. Links to other websites</h2>
                    <p>Our pages may link to third-party sites for convenience. We don't control those sites and aren't responsible for their content or policies.</p>

                    <h2>7. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
                    <p>This website is provided "as is". While we work hard to keep schedules and details accurate, sessions, speakers and venues can change — see section 3 of our Sales Policy for how we handle that.</p>

                    <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
                    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, AAAI Inc.'s total liability arising out of or relating to the website or the event is limited to the value of your pass (or zero if none was purchased).</p>

                    <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
                    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India, with courts in Mumbai having exclusive jurisdiction.</p>

                    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
                    <p>Questions about these terms? Write to <a href="mailto:hello@aaaihub.org">hello@aaaihub.org</a>.</p>
                </div>
            </section>
        </main>
        <EventFooter />
    </body>
</html>
